@startuml JSONL Logging System
title JSONL Logging System - ML Training Data Pipeline

package "Logging Sources" {
    component [SessionCoordinator] as Coord
    component [MechanicsEngine] as Mech
    component [DMAgent] as DM
    component [PlayerAgent] as Player
    component [EnemyAgent] as Enemy
}

package "JSONLLogger" {
    component [EventBuffer] as Buffer
    component [SchemaValidator] as Validator
    component [FileWriter] as Writer

    note right of Buffer
        10 Event Types:
        1. session_start
        2. scenario
        3. action_declaration
        4. action_resolution
        5. round_synthesis
        6. round_summary
        7. character_state
        8. combat_action
        9. enemy_spawn
        10. enemy_defeat
        11. mission_debrief
        12. llm_call
    end note
}

package "JSONL Output" {
    file "session_<timestamp>.jsonl" as JSONL
    file "game.log" as GameLog

    note right of JSONL
        Each line = 1 JSON event
        Example:
        {"event_type":"action_resolution",...}
        {"event_type":"character_state",...}

        Size: ~50KB - 5MB per session
        Duration: 1-20 rounds
    end note
}

package "Analysis Tools" {
    component [analyze_session.py] as Analyze
    component [extract_fixture.py] as Extract
    component [replay_fixture.py] as Replay
    component [diff_fixtures.py] as Diff
    component [validate_logging.py] as Validate
    component [reconstruct_narrative.py] as Reconstruct

    note bottom of Analyze
        Quick analysis tool:
        - Session summary
        - Event search/filter
        - Field extraction
        - Count/index modes
        (Use instead of reading huge JSONL!)
    end note
}

' Logging flow
Coord --> Buffer : log_session_start()
Coord --> Buffer : log_scenario()
Coord --> Buffer : log_round_synthesis()
Coord --> Buffer : log_round_summary()
Coord --> Buffer : log_mission_debrief()

Mech --> Buffer : log_action_declaration()
Mech --> Buffer : log_action_resolution()
Mech --> Buffer : log_character_state()
Mech --> Buffer : log_combat_action()
Mech --> Buffer : log_enemy_spawn()
Mech --> Buffer : log_enemy_defeat()

DM --> Buffer : (via Mech/Coord)
Player --> Buffer : (via Mech/Coord)
Enemy --> Buffer : (via Mech/Coord)

' Internal logger flow
Buffer --> Validator : validate_schema()
Validator --> Writer : write_event()
Writer --> JSONL : append line
Writer --> GameLog : log summary

' Analysis flow
JSONL --> Analyze : read
JSONL --> Extract : extract rounds
JSONL --> Validate : validate all
JSONL --> Reconstruct : rebuild story

Extract --> Replay : fixture input
Replay --> JSONL : new session output
Diff --> JSONL : compare before/after

== Event Flow Examples ==

participant Coord as Coord2
participant Mech as Mech2
participant Logger as Logger2
participant JSONL as JSONL2

note over Coord2, JSONL2: Session Start

Coord2 -> Logger2: log_session_start(config)
Logger2 -> JSONL2: {"event_type":"session_start","session_id":"...","config":{...}}

note over Coord2, JSONL2: DM Generates Scenario

Coord2 -> Logger2: log_scenario(scenario)
Logger2 -> JSONL2: {"event_type":"scenario","theme":"...","void_level":8,...}

note over Coord2, JSONL2: Player Action

Mech2 -> Logger2: log_action_declaration(action)
Logger2 -> JSONL2: {"event_type":"action_declaration","agent":"Ash","action":"..."}

Mech2 -> Logger2: log_action_resolution(resolution)
Logger2 -> JSONL2: {"event_type":"action_resolution","roll":{...},"effects":{...}}

note over Coord2, JSONL2: Character State Change

Mech2 -> Logger2: log_character_state(character)
Logger2 -> JSONL2: {"event_type":"character_state","hp":8,"void":3,"wounds":1}

note over Coord2, JSONL2: Round End

Coord2 -> Logger2: log_round_summary(summary)
Logger2 -> JSONL2: {"event_type":"round_summary","round":3,"summary":"..."}

== ML Training Use Cases ==

note right of JSONL
    Training scenarios:

    1. Action→Resolution mapping
       - Input: action_declaration
       - Output: action_resolution
       - Learn: DM adjudication patterns

    2. Tactical decision making
       - Input: combat_state + character_state
       - Output: enemy action
       - Learn: Enemy AI tactics

    3. Damage extraction
       - Input: narration text
       - Output: damage.dealt values
       - Learn: Parse effects from text

    4. Void progression
       - Input: scenario.void_level + actions
       - Output: void_changes over time
       - Learn: Corruption mechanics

    5. Story generation
       - Input: scenario.theme
       - Output: round_synthesis events
       - Learn: Narrative coherence
end note

@enduml
